<!--
  ============================================================================
  HuttEyes_RestoreRenderNodes.xml            Jawa_Patches · authored 2026-08-11
  ============================================================================

  THE OBSERVATION
  ===============
  Observed in game 2026-08-11 at full stack: Hutts have "little black eyelashed
  eyes" instead of the vertical slit pupils HuttEyes_Slitted.xml was supposed to
  give them. Verified from the live def dump: all six feline genes we assign have
  renderNodeProperties = NONE, while our own RimMandrake_Jawa_Eyes_HugeOrange still has 2.

  THE CAUSE  [the interesting part]
  =================================
  [LFS] Genes Expanded - Eyes ships Compatibility/FacialAnimation/1.5/Patches/
  FAFelineEyesPatch.xml, which does PatchOperationRemove on
  renderNodeProperties for EVERY feline gene. It is gated on Facial Animation
  being INSTALLED, not on the pawn being FA-driven — and FA is installed in this
  stack. The mod's reasoning is sound for its own use case: if FA paints the
  face, the gene's own eye art would double-draw, so it strips the node and hands
  FA a colour instead via its EyeballColorDef.

  But we deliberately EXCLUDED BTD_Hutt from Facial Animation so the slit art
  could show. So neither party draws an eye:

      LFS patch  -> gene has no render node, because FA is installed
      FA         -> not drawing this pawn, because we excluded the xenotype

  What is left is the Hutt head texture's own baked-in eyes. Hence eyelashes.

  ⚠️ 2026-08-12: RETARGETED FROM THE FELINE FAMILY TO THE REPTILE FAMILY.
  ==================================================================
  Owner's call after seeing the feline eyes in game (Steam screenshots
  20260812125725 / 125845). The art comparison and reasoning live in the sibling
  file HuttEyes_Slitted.xml — read it there, not here.

  What matters HERE is that the two files are ONE change and must move together.
  Verified against the live def dump (captured 2026-08-12T19:23:41Z, 568 mods):

    Eyes_<colour>_Feline   renderNodeProperties PRESENT  <- only because THIS
                                                            file restored them
    Eyes_<colour>_Reptile  renderNodeProperties STRIPPED <- nobody restored these

  So swapping the gene names in HuttEyes_Slitted.xml without also swapping them
  here hands BTD_Hutt six genes that draw nothing, and the Hutts render with no
  eyes at all — the exact failure this file exists to prevent, merely moved to a
  different family. All six ReptileEyes texPaths were confirmed to resolve to a
  real PNG on disk before the edit landed.

  BOTH families are restored below, on purpose. See the LEGACY FAMILY note at the
  second block: the xenotype rolls Reptile for new pawns, while already-generated
  pawns keep Feline in their saved data and would otherwise go eyeless.

  THE FIX
  =======
  Put the render nodes back on just the genes BTD_Hutt uses. Copied verbatim
  from the donor definitions in Versions/1.6/.../FelineEyes.xml, which is what
  the gene looks like when FA is absent — same anchorTag, layer 54, offset and
  the West flip handling on the left eye; texPath follows the family.

  drawSize is the ONE deliberate deviation from the donor: 0.21 raised to 0.42.

  0.55 WAS TRIED AND FAILED ON SCREEN, 2026-08-12. Six Hutts spawned live; the
  slit and the warm iris both read correctly and the colour varied per pawn, but
  the two eyes ABUTTED EDGE TO EDGE and read as one mass. Measured off the
  screenshot rather than judged by eye: each iris was ~51 px wide and the two
  centres were ~51.5 px apart, i.e. width == centre spacing, zero gap.

  Horizontal position is NOT ours to set - it comes from the head's RightEye /
  LeftEye anchorTags, and our offset is (0, 0, -0.25), vertical only. So the ONLY
  lever on separation is drawSize. At 0.42 the iris is ~39 px against the same
  ~51.5 px spacing, leaving a gap of about a quarter of an eye.

  ⛔ 0.42 WAS ALSO TRIED AND ALSO FAILED ON SCREEN, 2026-08-12 evening.
  =====================================================================
  **A quarter-eye gap does not read as two eyes.** Owner called it on sight;
  measurement then agreed. Six Hutts photographed south-on; on five of them the
  eyes read as ONE horizontal capsule with vertical striping - the same "one
  mass" failure 0.55 produced, merely less extreme.

  ⚠️ The geometry was doing exactly what this header predicted. Measured
  gap/iris was 0.36 against the ~0.32 predicted. **The patch was correct and the
  TARGET was wrong** - "a gap of about a quarter of an eye" is not a sufficient
  success condition, and it should never have been written as one.

  TWO reasons a quarter-eye gap fails, both visible only on a zoomed capture:
    1. Each iris carries a dark hourglass SLIT roughly as wide as the inter-eye
       gap, so the eye reads as four bright bars at near-even spacing rather
       than two eyes. The slit competes with the gap.
    2. The two eyes' dark OUTLINES touch, enclosing both irises in a single
       capsule. One outline reads as one object.

  ⚠️ A measurement can confirm the number and still miss the read. The first
  automated pass here reported "SEPARATED" by taking max() over gaps of 3,4,3 -
  a 1 px difference called a verdict. Any test whose pass and fail print the
  same thing is not a test. Demand that the inter-eye gap DOMINATE the slit gap
  (ratio >= 2.5), do not merely find it.

  NOW AT 0.37, which puts the gap at half an iris instead of a quarter. This is
  a COMPROMISE, not a proven fix - at 0.37 the gap is only ~2x the slit width,
  so it may still not resolve. Judge it on screen; do not assume it passed.

  ⚠️ THE LADDER TRADES SIZE AGAINST SEPARATION, and the owner wants size:
        0.42  gap/iris 0.32   apparent 0.097   FAILED on screen
        0.37  gap/iris 0.50   apparent 0.085   <- current, +9% vs Jawa
        0.28  gap/iris 1.00   apparent 0.064   certain read, but -18% vs Jawa
  0.28 is the only value that certainly resolves, and it lands BELOW the
  approved Jawa size on a much larger face - against the owner's "pretty huge"
  call. Do not go there without asking.

  ➡️ THE REAL FIX IS ART, NOT A NUMBER. The constraint is iris WIDTH against a
  spacing we cannot set, and ReptileEyes is explicitly "a wider, flatter oval" -
  the worst shape for this. A NARROWER, TALLER eye keeps apparent size while
  opening a horizontal gap, and escapes the ladder entirely. That is a retired seat's
  job and it is the only way to get both "huge" and "clearly two".
  on owner's call 2026-08-11, "they're supposed to be pretty huge". Hutts are the
  largest xenotype in the stack (guy762_BodySizeGene_biggest) and the donor value
  is tuned for a baseline human head, so the stock size read as small on that face.

  Jawa_Patches loads at 562 and the LFS mod at 420, so our Add lands after their
  Remove. Order matters absolutely here: reversed, this would be a silent no-op.

  ⚠️ SCOPE. This edits genes shared with any other xenotype that uses them. In
  this load only BTD_Hutt carries them, so the blast radius is Hutts. If another
  xenotype ever adopts a feline eye gene AND is FA-driven, it would double-draw:
  FA's painted eye plus the restored node. The correct fix then is to exclude
  that xenotype from FA too, exactly as we did for the Hutt.

  SETTLED 2026-08-13 BY THE OWNER - drawSize is 0.30. Do not walk the ladder.
  ====================================================================
  The ladder that used to live here (0.55 -> 0.45 -> 0.38) is spent, and it is
  deleted rather than left as a stale instruction: every rung is now ABOVE the
  shipped value, so following it would only ever make the eyes bigger again.

  SEEN ON SCREEN first, then ruled. Two dev-spawned Hutts (Natal, Shad) at 0.37
  on the 574 stack: two clearly separate eyes, vertical slit pupils, warm iris
  colour, no eyelashes - so the reptile swap and the FA exclusion both work, and
  the ONLY outstanding complaint was size. Owner called another 20% down and
  said ship it: 0.37 x 0.8 = 0.296, shipped as 0.30 to match the two-decimal
  convention used throughout this file (a 19% drop).

  There is no open question here. If a future session thinks the eyes are wrong,
  that is a NEW judgement needing a NEW screenshot - not a resumption of this
  one.

  SIZING MATH, so the next change is not a guess. Apparent size = drawSize x the
  eye's share of its canvas. The LFS art puts a 38px eye in a 168px canvas, only
  23%, whereas our own Jawa art is 49% — which is why the donor's 0.21 looked
  like eyelashes while the Jawa's 0.16 looked right.

      Jawa  0.16 x 49% = 0.078   (approved)
      Hutt  0.42 x 23% = 0.095   (1.22x Jawa - still small on a much larger face)
      Hutt  0.55 x 23% = 0.124   (1.59x Jawa - chosen)
      Hutt  0.70 x 23% = 0.158   (2.03x Jawa - if it still reads small)
    * Still no eyebrows — that is the FA exclusion and is expected.
    * If they now have TWO sets of eyes, the FA exclusion for BTD_Hutt was lost.
  ============================================================================
-->
